{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Finite","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Nat","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.GetD"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct_pos","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L144-L149","doc":"The hook-length product is positive (a product of positive hook lengths). This makes the\nFRT formula's division form `f^μ = |μ|! / ∏ h_c` well-posed and is what the multiplicative\nstatement `HookProductHLF.numSYT_mul_hookProduct` is divided through by. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L140-L142","doc":"The **hook-length product** `∏_{c ∈ μ} h(c)` appearing in the FRT formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hookLength_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hookLength_pos","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L134-L136","doc":"Every hook length is positive: besides its arm and leg it counts the cell itself (`+ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.hookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.hookLength","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L127-L132","doc":"The **hook length** of cell `(i, j)` in `μ`: arm (cells strictly to the right in\nrow `i`) + leg (cells strictly below in column `j`) + the cell itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.numSYT_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.numSYT_bot","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L106-L125","doc":"Base case: the empty diagram has a single standard tableau (the empty filling),\nso `numSYT ⊥ = 1`. This also confirms the `zero_off` normalisation makes `numSYT`\ncount correctly — without it the type would be infinite and `Nat.card` would give\n`0`, not `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.numSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.numSYT","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L92-L104","doc":"`numSYT μ = #SYT(μ)`, the number of standard Young tableaux of shape `μ`.\nThis is the dimension `f^μ = dim V_μ` of the irreducible `S_{|μ|}`-representation\nindexed by `μ` (program brick 1 / phase P2). Well-defined because\n`StandardYoungTableau μ` is finite (the `zero_off` normalisation pins entries off\nthe diagram, so an SYT is determined by its finitely many on-cell values).\nNoncomputable: it counts an unbundled structure via `Nat.card`, which is a genuine count\nhere because `StandardYoungTableau.instFinite` (above) proves the type finite.\n\nThe brick-1 FRT identity is **proved** downstream as\n`QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.numSYT_mul_hookProduct` (see the note at the end of this\nfile for why it cannot be stated here). The `Finite` instance and the base case\n`numSYT ⊥ = 1` — `numSYT_bot` — are proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.instFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.instFinite","kind":"instance","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L83-L88","doc":"`StandardYoungTableau μ` is **finite**: an SYT is determined by its finitely many on-cell\nentries (`encode` is injective into `{c // c ∈ μ.cells} → Fin μ.card`). This makes `numSYT`\nbelow (a `Nat.card`) a genuine count, rather than the `0` fallback that `Nat.card` returns on\nan infinite type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.encode_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.encode_injective","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L74-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.encode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.encode","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L67-L72","doc":"Encode a standard tableau by its entries on the cells of `μ`: each on-cell entry lies in\n`Fin μ.card` (by `lt_card`), and `zero_off` pins the off-cell entries to `0`, so a tableau is\nfully determined by this finite data. This injection into a finite function type witnesses\nfiniteness of `StandardYoungTableau μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.col_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.col_strict","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Entries strictly increase down each column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.row_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.row_strict","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Entries strictly increase along each row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.inj_on","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.inj_on","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Distinct cells carry distinct entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.zero_off","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.zero_off","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Off the diagram the filling is pinned to `0`, so the structure is finite (an\nSYT is determined by its values on the finitely many cells of `μ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.lt_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.lt_card","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Entries lie in `{0, …, |μ| − 1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.entry","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The entry at cell `(i, j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.mk","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.ext","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.ext_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.ext_iff","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau","kind":"structure","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L37-L61","doc":"A **standard Young tableau** of shape `μ`: a filling of the cells of `μ` by the\nintegers `0, …, |μ| − 1`, each used once, strictly increasing along rows\n(left → right) and down columns (top → bottom). Entries are carried by\n`entry : ℕ → ℕ → ℕ`, constrained on the cells `(i, j) ∈ μ` and pinned to `0` off the\ndiagram (`zero_off`) so the type is **finite** — an SYT is fully determined by its\nvalues on the finitely many cells of `μ` — which is what makes `numSYT` via\n`Nat.card` well-defined (without `zero_off` the entry field would be free off-cells,\nthe type infinite, and `Nat.card` would collapse to `0`). Surjectivity onto\n`{0, …, |μ| − 1}` is *omitted*: it is forced by `inj_on` together with\n`μ.cells.card = μ.card`, so stating it would be redundant. ","signatureChunk":0}]}